Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.00,0:00:20.57,Kick,,0,0,0,,ZEPTO · EXPLAINED
Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.00,0:00:20.57,Title,,0,0,0,,10 MINUTES.\NNOT THE RIDER.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.00,0:00:20.57,Foot,,0,0,0,,Source: Aadit Palicha via Global Indian\NFull video on the channel
Dialogue: 1,0:00:00.15,0:00:02.40,Big,,0,0,0,,{\pos(540,1640)\fad(120,150)}UNDER 15 KM/H
Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.00,0:00:01.90,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}Zepto delivers in ten minutes.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:01.90,0:00:04.10,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}And its riders are not riding fast.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:04.10,0:00:05.60,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}Here is the trick.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:05.70,0:00:10.15,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}Each dark store covers a small radius, so the rider only has a short distance to go.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:10.15,0:00:16.55,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}Aadit Palicha once pointed out that covering 1.8 kilometres in ten minutes means riding under fifteen kilometres an hour.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:16.55,0:00:20.57,Cap,,0,0,0,,{\fad(60,60)}The speed comes from where the store sits, not from how fast the rider goes.
